{"path":"chrono/last_spec","title":"std::chrono::last_spec, std::chrono::last","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::chrono::</span>last_spec, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::chrono::</span>last","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/chrono/last_spec","section":"chrono","kind":"page","summary":"last_spec is an empty tag type that is used in conjunction with other calendar types to indicate the last thing in a sequence.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/chrono\">&lt;chrono&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> last_spec<br><span class=\"br0\">{</span><br>&nbsp; &nbsp; <span class=\"kw1\">explicit</span> last_spec<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"kw1\">default</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span><br><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx20\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">inline</span> <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> last_spec last<span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx20\">(since C++20)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>last_spec</code> is an empty tag type that is used in conjunction with other calendar types to indicate the last thing in a sequence. Depending on context, it may indicate the last day of a month (as in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">2018y<span class=\"sy2\">/</span>February<span class=\"sy2\">/</span>last</span></code>, for last day of February 2018, i.e., 2018-02-28) or the last day of the week in a month (as in <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"nu0\">2018</span><span class=\"sy2\">/</span>February<span class=\"sy2\">/</span>Sunday<span class=\"br0\">[</span>last<span class=\"br0\">]</span></span></code>, for last Sunday of February 2018, i.e., 2018-02-25).\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;chrono&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">using</span> <span class=\"kw1\">namespace</span> std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">chrono</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> mdl <span class=\"br0\">{</span>June<span class=\"sy2\">/</span>last<span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    static_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span>mdl <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> month_day_last<span class=\"br0\">(</span>month<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw4\">constexpr</span> <span class=\"kw4\">auto</span> ymwdl <span class=\"br0\">{</span>year<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2023</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">/</span>December<span class=\"sy2\">/</span>Tuesday<span class=\"br0\">[</span>last<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    static_assert<span class=\"br0\">(</span>ymwdl <span class=\"sy1\">==</span>\n        year_month_weekday_last<span class=\"br0\">(</span>year<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">2023</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, month<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"nu0\">12</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, weekday_last<span class=\"br0\">(</span>Tuesday<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n</div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"chrono","title":"Date and time utilities"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::chrono::last_spec, std::chrono::last","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"2 declarations; revisions: since C++20. last_spec is an empty tag type that is used in conjunction with other calendar types to indicate the last thing in a…"},{"label":"Example"}]},"standards":["C++20"],"wordCount":111,"codeBlockCount":1}
